# Hand-written PDBx/mmCIF, not an archive entry.
#
# What it demonstrates: `_struct_conn` states a disulfide, and the reader builds it because the file
# states it -- not because two sulphurs happen to be close.  Two CYS monomers of one polymer chain,
# each fully bonded from `_chem_comp_bond` (5 bonds, one of them the C=O double), joined SG-SG.
# It also demonstrates the boundary: the peptide bond between monomer 1 and monomer 2 is NOT stated
# as a pair of atoms anywhere in mmCIF, so it is not built and the log says so.
#
# The coordinates are deliberately not a real geometry: CB and SG of monomer 2 are 3.8 A
# apart, past every cutoff any toolkit uses, and the bond is still built.  Nothing in this
# reader looks at a distance.
data_TESTSS
_entry.id   TESTSS
_struct.title   'two cysteines, one stated disulfide'
#
loop_
_entity.id
_entity.type
1 polymer
